meta {
  name: Ask (RAG)
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/rag/ask?q=Who won the world cup in 1998?
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  q: Who won the world cup in 1998?
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.answer: isString
}

docs {
  The FULL RAG loop: retrieve -> augment the prompt -> generate (DeepSeek).
  Returns { question, answer, sources[] } — the grounded answer PLUS the chunks
  it stood on, so you can audit it.
  
  Prerequisites:
    - DEEPSEEK_API_KEY in .env for a GENERATED answer. Without it the app still
      boots and this returns the retrieved sources + a "chat not configured" note.
    - Run "Ingest Sample" first so there's something to retrieve.
  Try a question the docs DON'T cover (like this 1998 World Cup one) to watch it
  say "I don't know" instead of hallucinating — the prompt-template rule at work.
}
